  clock: 8  # e8d8
  nonce: e8d8  # e8d8
  message: "Fixed in PR #699 (merged, dev 5b8a44805f). ROOT CAUSE (chokepoint, not per-site): the INV-sotiv backstop populate_kind_stable_ids covered {interface,type} but not the other container/declaration kinds; the tree-sitter producers construct class/struct/enum/trait/protocol/contract with shape_id= but no stable_id=, so they fell through to None. FIX: new make_declaration_stable_id (file-scoped sha256(kind:language:path:name), kind threaded in so class vs same-named struct stay distinct) + registered the 6 container kinds in _KIND_STABLE_ID_FACTORIES — one place, every analyzer. Producer-computed ids (Python classes via _compute_stable_id) keep precedence; backstop only fills None. BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE (re-ran the item's own filed widget.ts repro via hypergumbo survey): class ItemDetail None->sha256:a5ec36a31d4a7d2b, enum Color None->sha256:e3950472c3f2c0ab; interface/type unchanged. Cross-language survey: go struct/interface, rust enum/struct/trait, solidity contract all now populated. Production-path test test_kind_stable_id_coverage.py::TestContainerKindEndToEnd (orchestrator on a TS fixture) + unit tests; base.py 100% cov, 10119 tests green on targeted manifest. RESIDUAL (correctly out of scope — callable kinds must not use the name-scoped backstop, they need a TYPED producer id or they collide across overloads): solidity function/constructor + go interface-method declarations still emit stable_id=None -> filed WI-vibad-lajoz-jifut-zalad-sodad-bumab-dinij-vupif."  # e8d8
